
# Jenkins CI/CD Task 2

### Automated CI/CD Pipeline with Jenkins and Docker

A Node.js application demonstrating an automated **Build → Test → Deploy** CI/CD workflow using **Jenkins** and **Docker**.

[![Jenkins](https://img.shields.io/badge/Jenkins-CI%2FCD-D24939?logo=jenkins&logoColor=white)](http://localhost:8080/)
[![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-Containerized-2496ED?logo=docker&logoColor=white)](https://www.docker.com/)
[![Node.js](https://img.shields.io/badge/Node.js-22-339933?logo=node.js&logoColor=white)](https://nodejs.org/)

**Repository:** [GitHub](https://github.com/sakthi2300/jenkins-cicd-task-2)

---

## Overview

This project demonstrates how to automate the **build, testing, and deployment** of a Node.js application using **Jenkins** and **Docker**.

Whenever a new code change is pushed to the `main` branch, Jenkins periodically checks the GitHub repository using **Poll SCM** and automatically starts the pipeline when a new commit is detected.

The Jenkins pipeline automatically:

* Checks out the source code from GitHub.
* Builds a Docker image using the project's Dockerfile.
* Tests the Node.js application's JavaScript syntax.
* Deploys the application as a Docker container.
* Makes the application available on port `3000`.

This project demonstrates the fundamentals of **CI/CD automation, Jenkins pipelines, Git integration, and Docker-based application deployment**.

## CI/CD Workflow

```text
              Code Push to Main
                     |
                     v
              GitHub Repository
                     |
                     v
              Jenkins Poll SCM
              (Every ~5 minutes)
                     |
                     v
              Checkout Source
                     |
                     v
              Build Docker Image
                     |
                     v
                Test Stage
             (node --check)
                     |
                     v
              Deploy Container
                     |
                     v
          Node.js Application
           localhost:3000
```

### Pipeline Stages

| Stage | Description |
| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Trigger | Jenkins Poll SCM checks the GitHub repository for new commits. |
| Checkout | Retrieves the source code from the GitHub repository. |
| Build | Builds the Docker image using the project's Dockerfile. |
| Test | Checks the Node.js application's JavaScript syntax using `node --check server.js`. |
| Deploy | Runs the Docker container and exposes the application on port `3000`. |
| Post Actions | Displays a success or failure message after pipeline execution. |

## Technology Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
| -------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Node.js 22 | JavaScript runtime |
| Express.js | Web application framework |
| Docker | Application containerization |
| Jenkins | CI/CD automation |
| Git | Version control |
| GitHub | Source code hosting |
| Groovy | Jenkins Pipeline syntax |

